This is what my AI said:

Marina Alta, facing severe droughts and discharging over 70% of its treated
wastewater into the sea, can learn from the Orange County Water District
<https://www.ocwd.com/>. OCWD manages one of the world's most advanced
basins by combining massive indirect potable reuse and strict aquifer
protection. [1 <https://www.ocwd.com/what-we-do/groundwater-management/>, 2
<https://rua.ua.es/dspace/bitstream/10045/155145/1/Sanchez-Perez_Lopez-Orti=
z_2025_Sustainability.pdf>,
3
<https://cacoastkeeper.org/ocean-desalination-is-not-needed-in-orange-count=
y/>,
4 <https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=3DYgWDlpFGnzo>, 5
<https://www.mdpi.com/2071-1050/17/12/5512>]
Transitioning from crisis-mode to long-term security requires adopting
three main pillars:
1. Unified Water Governance

   - *The OCWD Model:* Governed by a single consolidated Board of Directors
   <https://www.ocwd.com/about/service-area-board-of-directors/> that
   actively manages, replenishes, and protects the overarching groundwater
   basin. [1 <https://www.ocwd.com/about/service-area-board-of-directors/>]
   - *Marina Alta Application:* The local *Consorcio de Abastecimiento y
   Saneamiento de Aguas (CASAMA)* has remained largely inoperative. Marina
   Alta must operationalize a single, centralized water authority to pool
   resources and end the fragmented, municipal-level management that falter=
s
   during shortages. [1 <https://www.mdpi.com/2071-1050/17/12/5512>, 2
   <https://ideas.repec.org/a/gam/jsusta/v17y2025i12p5512-d1679493.html>]

2. Advanced Water Reuse (Circular Economy)

   - *The OCWD Model:* Operates the Groundwater Replenishment System
   (GWRS), the world's largest water purification project for indirect pota=
ble
   reuse. Highly treated wastewater undergoes microfiltration, reverse
   osmosis, and ultraviolet light, then gets injected into basins or coasta=
l
   barriers. [1 <https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=3DjGa31U9v9No>, 2
   <https://www.ocwd.com/gwrs/the-process/>, 3
   <https://www.sandiego.gov/sites/default/files/legacy/water/pdf/purewater=
/090625challengeswaterrecycling.pdf>,
   4 <https://www.ocwd.com/what-we-do/water-reuse/>, 5
   <https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=3D12u0ENQNruU>]
   - *Marina Alta Application:* Marina Alta treats 15.1 hm=C2=B3 of water
   annually, but a staggering 70.87% goes straight into the sea, with a mea=
ger
   1.82% reused for agriculture. Instead of relying on expensive,
   energy-intensive coastal desalination, local plants (like the one in
   Teulada=E2=80=93Moraira) should upgrade to advanced reverse osmosis and =
UV
   treatment so reclaimed water can safely recharge aquifers or irrigate th=
e
   region's agricultural lands. [1
   <https://www.researchgate.net/figure/Distribution-of-water-resources-in-=
La-Marina-Alta-district-in-2014-Source-own_fig1_392756069>,
   2
   <https://rua.ua.es/dspace/bitstream/10045/155145/1/Sanchez-Perez_Lopez-O=
rtiz_2025_Sustainability.pdf>,
   3
   <https://cacoastkeeper.org/ocean-desalination-is-not-needed-in-orange-co=
unty/>
   ]

3. Aquifer Protection & Seawater Barriers

   - *The OCWD Model:* Manages extensive Groundwater Supplies
   <https://www.ocwd.com/what-we-do/groundwater-management/groundwater-supp=
lies/>
   via 400 district-owned monitoring wells, preventing seawater intrusion a=
nd
   over-extraction through strict scientific modeling and injection barrier=
s.
   [1 <https://www.ocwd.com/what-we-do/groundwater-management/>, 2
   <https://www.ocwd.com/what-we-do/groundwater-management/groundwater-supp=
lies/>,
   3 <https://www.ocwd.com/roy-herndon-chief-hydrogeologist/>, 4
   <https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=3DL2HA0Mg8PA4>, 5
   <https://www.ocwd.com/wp-content/uploads/groundwatermanagementplan2015up=
date_20150624.pdf>
   ]
   - *Marina Alta Application:* Prolonged droughts and tourist booms have
   severely overexploited local coastal aquifers. Implementing OCWD's
   continuous monitoring network would allow authorities to track subterran=
ean
   water tables and inject purified wastewater to maintain hydraulic pressu=
re,
   keeping saltwater out of freshwater wells. [1
   <https://www.ocwd.com/what-we-do/groundwater-management/>, 2
   <https://www.mdpi.com/2071-1050/17/12/5512>, 3
   <https://costablanca-magazin.com/en/local/information/water-shortage-on-=
the-costa-blanca-urgent-measures-in-the-municipalities/>,
   4 <https://www.ocwd.com/roy-herndon-chief-hydrogeologist/>]

